e Bench v5.29.1\n  59 \n  60 \u2705 **Database & Cache**\n  61 - MariaDB Server 10.11.14\n  62 - Redis Server 7.0.15\n  63 \n  64 \u2705 **Tools & Dependencies**\n  65 - Python 3.12.12 (virtual environment)\n  66 - Node.js v22.14.0, npm 10.9.2, Yarn 1.22.22\n  67 - wkhtmltopdf, Supervisor, Cron daemon\n  68 - All required system libraries\n  69 \n  70 \u2705 **Pre-configured Site**\n  71 - Site name: `frappe.local`\n  72 - Admin user: `Administrator`\n  73 - Database: Automatically configured\n  74 \n  75 ---\n  76 \n  77 ## \ud83d\ude80 Common Tasks\n  78 \n  79 ### Start the Server\n  80 ```bash\n  81 cd ~/frappe-bench\n  82 bench start\n  83 ```\n  84 \n  85 ### Create Another Site\n  86 ```bash\n  87 bench new-site mysite.local --admin-password=PASSWORD\n  88 ```\n  89 \n  90 ### Install an App\n  91 ```bash\n  92 bench --site frappe.local install-app app_name\n  93 ```\n  94 \n  95 ### View Logs\n  96 ```bash\n  97 bench logs -f\n  98 ```\n  99 \n 100 ### Access the Database\n 101 ```bash\n 102 sudo mysql -u root -pfrappe@123\n 103 ```\n 104 \n 105 ### Run Tests\n 106 ```bash\n 107 bench --site frappe.local run-tests\n 108 ```\n 109 \n 110 ---\n 111 \n 112 ## \ud83d\udd27 Services Running\n 113 \n 114 | Service | Port | Status |\n 115 |---------|------|--------|\n 116 | Frappe Web Server | 8000 | \u2713 Ready |\n 117 | MariaDB | 3306 | \u2713 Active |\n 118 | Redis | 6379 | \u2713 Active |\n 119 | WebSocket | 9000 | \u2713 Ready (when server starts) |\n 120 \n 121 ---\n 122 \n 123 ## \ud83d\udcd6 For More Information\n 124 \n 125 See the detailed documentation files:\n 126 \n 127 1. **FRAPPE_SETUP_SUMMARY.md** - Complete guide with all details\n 128 2. **QUICK_REFERENCE.md** - Common commands and troubleshooting\n 129 3. **INSTALLATION_VERIFICATION.md** - What was verified during installation\n 130 \n 131 Or visit:\n 132 - Official Docs: https://frappeframework.com/docs/\n 133 - GitHub: https://github.com/frappe/frappe\n 134 - Forum: https://discuss.erpnext.com/\n 135 \n 136 ---\n 137 \n 138 ## \u2705 Verification Checklist\n 139 \n 140 All items verified as complete:\n 141 - [x] System requirements met\n 142 - [x] Database configured and running\n 143 - [x] Cache server configured and running\n 144 - [x] Frappe Framework installed\n 145 - [x] Site created and initialized\n 146 - [x] Assets compiled\n 147 - [x] Services running\n 148 - [x] Documentation created\n 149 \n 150 ---\n 151 \n 152 ## \u26a0\ufe0f Before Production\n 153 \n 154 Your current setup is ideal for development. Before deploying to production:\n 155 \n 156 1. Change all default passwords\n 157 2. Set up SSL/TLS certificates\n 158 3. Configure Nginx reverse proxy\n 159 4. Set up automated backups\n 160 5. Configure firewall rules\n 161 6. Enable proper logging and monitoring\n 162 \n 163 See FRAPPE_SETUP_SUMMARY.md for detailed production checklist.\n 164 \n 165 ---\n 166 \n 167 ## \ud83c\udfaf Next Steps\n 168 \n 169 1. **Today:** Start the server and explore the interface\n 170 2. **This week:** Learn Frappe architecture and create custom apps\n 171 3. **When ready:** Deploy to production following the security checklist\n 172 \n 173 ---\n 174 \n 175 **You're all set! Happy coding! \ud83d\ude80**\n 176 \n 177 Questions? Check the documentation files or visit the Frappe forum.\n 178 \n````", "Successfully opened frappe-bench/apps/frappe/README.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 <div align=\"center\">\n   1 \t<h1>\n   2 \t\t<br>\n   3 \t\t<a href=\"https://frappeframework.com\">\n   4 \t\t\t<img src=\".github/frappe-framework-logo.svg\" height=\"50\">\n   5 \t\t</a>\n   6 \t</h1>\n   7 \t<h3>\n   8 \t\ta web framework with <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LOjk3m0wTwg\">\"batteries included\"</a>\n   9 \t</h3>\n  10 \t<h5>\n  11 \t\tit's pronounced - <em>fra-pay</em>\n  12 \t</h5>\n  13 </div>\n  14 \n  15 <div align=\"center\">\n  16 \t<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"#LICENSE\" title=\"License: MIT\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-succes