h/tree/develop#easy-install-script)\n  45 * [Manual install using Docker images](https://github.com/frappe/frappe_docker)\n  46 \n  47 ### Development\n  48 * [Easy install script using Docker images](https://github.com/frappe/bench/tree/develop#easy-install-script)\n  49 * [Development installation on bare metal](https://frappeframework.com/docs/user/en/installation)\n  50 \n  51 \n  52 ## Contributing\n  53 \n  54 1. [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n  55 1. [Contribution Guidelines](https://github.com/frappe/erpnext/wiki/Contribution-Guidelines)\n  56 1. [Security Policy](SECURITY.md)\n  57 1. [Translations](https://translate.erpnext.com)\n  58 \n  59 ## Resources\n  60 \n  61 1. [frappeframework.com](https://frappeframework.com) - Official documentation of the Frappe Framework.\n  62 1. [frappe.school](https://frappe.school) - Pick from the various courses by the maintainers or from the community.\n  63 \n  64 ## License\n  65 This repository has been released under the [MIT License](LICENSE).\n  66 \n  67 By contributing to Frappe, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under its MIT License.\n  68 \n````", "Successfully opened frappe-bench/apps/frappe/pyproject.toml:\n\n````toml\n   0 [project]\n   1 name = \"frappe\"\n   2 authors = [\n   3     { name = \"Frappe Technologies Pvt Ltd\", email = \"developers@frappe.io\"}\n   4 ]\n   5 description = \"Metadata driven, full-stack low code web framework\"\n   6 requires-python = \">=3.10,<3.14\"\n   7 readme = \"README.md\"\n   8 dynamic = [\"version\"]\n   9 dependencies = [\n  10     # core dependencies\n  11     \"Babel~=2.13.1\",\n  12     \"Click~=8.2.0\",\n  13     \"filelock~=3.20.1\",\n  14     \"filetype~=1.2.0\",\n  15     \"GitPython~=3.1.34\",\n  16     \"Jinja2~=3.1.2\",\n  17     \"Pillow~=11.3.0\",\n  18     \"PyJWT~=2.8.0\",\n  19     # We depend on internal attributes,\n  20     # do NOT add loose requirements on PyMySQL versions.\n  21     \"PyMySQL==1.1.1\",\n  22     \"pypdf==6